{"title":"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 36","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_36&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which of the following methods of proving a geometric figure a locus is not correct? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/7/5b73b94ea48f4dd7bdcfa2d3c2b2714f8cdc3089.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\text{Every point of the locus satisfies the conditions and every point not on the locus does}\\\\ \\text{not satisfy the conditions.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"659\" height=\"36\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/2/9d2c2b97823ab9ddba295da0e47eddc03fcd9173.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\text{Every point not satisfying the conditions is not on the locus and every point on the locus}\\\\ \\text{does satisfy the conditions.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"683\" height=\"36\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/6/d96645161990b2caa3a5881c12ef7736b9f96e4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\text{Every point satisfying the conditions is on the locus and every point on the locus satisfies}\\\\ \\text{the conditions.}$\" width=\"686\" height=\"33\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/5/b250b5c34bf11a7201c6ced114418fe81ea333b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{Every point not on the locus does not satisfy the conditions and every point not satisfying}\\\\ \\text{the conditions is not on the locus.}$\" width=\"694\" height=\"33\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/2/ce2fdc2aeedbf64391fcb4917bf5839f42b6149d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{Every point satisfying the conditions is on the locus and every point not satisfying the} \\\\ \\text{conditions is not on the locus.}$\" width=\"662\" height=\"33\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_36&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Statement <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a2194b81820e8380be586c1564c3f5d03d5c100d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" /> is wrong because it does not imply that all points that satisfy the conditions are on the locus.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_36&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME\" title=\"1951 AHSME\">1951 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1951 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1951\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_35\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems/Prob